    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cernŭo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. and n.
		cernuus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to throw</i> or <i>fall head
			foremost</i> (only ante- and post-class.), Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 21, 8</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 1, 19, p. 111, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Front. Princ. Hist. 5</span></i>.—In <i>dep.</i> form: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tigres cernuantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus de industriā cernuatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 45</span></i>
			.</div>
